The [public Contactly overview](https://aylith-labs.github.io/contactly/) explains this source-run project. It is a **static information page**, not a hosted contact app, account, or reminder service. This September media study documents actual local product UI; it does not change the separate June source milestone.

## One fictional person, five real UI states

Contactly ran locally against disposable SQLite with three invented contacts and `.example.test` email addresses. The API and web app were bound to loopback. The light and dark captures below show unmodified product pixels. “Cedar Rowan,” the workshop note, and the October follow-up are **fictional fixture data**, not private contact records.

